 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The forward pass involves $N \times n$ evaluations of the decoder for initial sampling, where $N$ is the number of pixels and $n$ is the number of samples per ray [S1, S3, unofficial]. The secant refinement adds $N \times n_{\text{secant\_steps}}$ evaluations [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The forward pass involves $N \times n$ evaluations of the decoder for initial sampling, where $N$ is the number of pixels and $n$ is the number of samples per ray [S1, unofficial][S3]. The bisection refinement adds $N \times n_{\text{secant\_steps}}$ evaluations [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Complexity:** Memory usage is constrained by the `max_points` parameter, which limits the number of points loaded to GPU memory per batch [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Trained on a single NVIDIA V100 GPU with a batch size of 64 images and 1024 pixels each [S2][S3, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Differentiable rendering allows for end-to-end training from single-view images without explicit 3D supervision [S3, unofficial].
