 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** The DVR method was introduced by Mescheder et al. in "Occupancy Networks: Learning 3D Reconstruction in Function Space" (CVPR 2019) and extended by Niemeyer et al. in "Differentiable Volumetric Rendering: Learning Implicit 3D Representations without 3D Supervision" (CVPR 2020) [S1, S3, unofficial].
-*   **History:** The method builds on the concept of occupancy networks, which represent 3D shapes as implicit functions [S1, S3, unofficial]. The differentiable rendering component allows these implicit representations to be trained from 2D images [S1, S3, unofficial].
-*   **Usage:** DVR is used for 3D shape and texture reconstruction from single-view or multi-view images, particularly in scenarios where 3D supervision is unavailable [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Origin:** The DVR method was introduced by Mescheder et al. in "Occupancy Networks: Learning 3D Reconstruction in Function Space" (CVPR 2019) and extended by Niemeyer et al. in "Differentiable Volumetric Rendering: Learning Implicit 3D Representations without 3D Supervision" (CVPR 2020) [S1, unofficial][S3].
+*   **History:** The method builds on the concept of occupancy networks, which represent 3D shapes as implicit functions [S1, unofficial][S3]. The differentiable rendering component allows these implicit representations to be trained from 2D images [S1, unofficial][S3].
